RECORDED DEVIATIONS (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Output path: the prompt's "Output" lists apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Battery/**, but the
   established BUILDING convention (every DONE sibling: BatteryCellsPage, PresetGallery,
   admin/*, analytics/*) lives under apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Feature>/**, which project.yml
   globs into the iOS + macOS app targets. Files placed there so xcodegen enumerates them
   (verified: all 12 files in the generated pbxproj). Same disposition as BatteryCellsPage.
2. Second data source ported: the manifest lists only `useEnergyFlow`, but the web page ALSO
   drives every summary card / chart / table / period off an inline `useQuery(['energy-stats'])`
   → GET /vehicles/{id}/energy?days=N. Narrowing to just the live flow would gut 20 of the 22
   panels (covenant #2). Both seam methods are implemented; the named web hook `useEnergyFlow`
   is kept verbatim at the Swift call site, and the inline query is mirrored as `useEnergyStats`.
3. Phase driver: the page phase (loading/empty/error/success) is driven by the historical
   stats source (web `isLoading`/`!stats`), exactly as the web is. The live flow is best-effort
   (web `retry:false`) — a throw/absent snapshot leaves it nil and the flow section shows its
   "No live data" / "N/A" fallbacks, never gating the page or surfacing an error (web parity).
4. Live-field units: the /energy/flow fields (dc/ac charging power → kW, energy_remaining → kWh)
   are rendered by the web VERBATIM with their kW/kWh labels (this endpoint is not routed through
   `useUnits`). Reproduced verbatim for numeric parity. The HISTORICAL stats source IS SI (Wh, m,
   Wh/m) and converts at the render boundary via the shared `Units` facade (ADR-005); efficiency
   converts inline (×1000 / ×1609.344) exactly as the web does.
5. Staleness chip ADDED (ADR-013): the live flow is a realtime query; a `> 2 min` staleness chip
   (EnergyFlowPageModel.isFlowStale / staleAfter=120s) was added — an enhancement over the web,
   which silently refetches. Surfaced with the existing "No live data" string + a clock glyph.
6. Error state ADDED (ADR-013 "never a blank region"): the web renders its empty state when the
   stats query rejects; a distinct retryable error region (TSErrorDisplay + Retry) was added.
   The 4 REQUIRED states (loading/empty/error/success) are all implemented.
7. Range control: the web header `RangePicker` (presetsOnly: today/7d/30d/90d/mtd/ytd) is
   reproduced as a native `TSSelect` over `EnergyRangePreset`; its 6 chip labels were added to the
   string catalog (additive, web `DATE_PRESETS[].fallback` verbatim). Plus the `VehicleSelect`
   (web `actions`) as a `TSSelect` over the vehicle list — both header actions reproduced.
8. Route registration: `/energy-flow` is a real top-level web route (App.tsx line 515, sidebar
   "Energy Flow"). Added an `energyFlow` AppRoute case (pathSegment `energy-flow`, group `.energy`)
   + an EnergyFlowRouteRegistration wired into the shell host registry — the same shape as the
   sibling `.batteryCells` route. AppRouteParser resolves `/energy-flow` automatically.

