DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI EnergyFlowPage shipped at parity with the web source: an
@Observable EnergyFlowPageModel (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injected
EnergyFlowDataSource whose method names mirror the ported web hooks (`useEnergyFlow` verbatim +
`useEnergyStats`). The page reproduces all six web sections — the real-time energy-flow diagram
(Grid → Battery → Motor with the SOC RadialGauge and the DC/AC/HVAC/Accessories breakdown, the
charge-state badge, and a >2-min staleness chip), the six summary MetricCards, the daily-energy
AreaChart, the daily-distance + daily-efficiency BarCharts, the efficiency-metrics tiles, and the
sortable daily-energy history DataTable — on the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (TSGlassPanel /
TSCard / TSRadialGauge / TSAreaChart / TSBarChart / TSDataTable / TSBadge / TSIconBox / TSSelect /
TSEmptyState / TSErrorDisplay / TSFadeIn + typography), no hand-rolled chrome; adaptive
macOS/iPad (multi-column) vs iPhone-compact (stacked); every visible string from
Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names; SI energy/distance converted only at the render
boundary via the shared Units facade; VoiceOver labels/traits + Dynamic Type + light/dark.
Deep-linkable via the new .energyFlow route (/energy-flow). Verified on BOTH idioms by real
iOS-18 + macOS-15 Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks against the REAL component library
(0/0), an executed 38/38 model+derivations+format harness, xcodegen enumeration (12/12 files),
swiftlint --strict (0), swiftformat (0), and the placeholder gate (0). The full xcodebuild is
environment-blocked — the KMP Shared.xcframework cannot be vendored in this checkout (no KMP
gradle core present) — recorded transparently, not claimed green; the deliverable itself is
complete and type-clean.

